/**
 * THE OSD PREVIEW BACKGROUND - a photograph, and nothing else.
 *
 * WHAT THIS IS. A still frame the operator supplied so the OSD preview
 * can be judged the way it will actually be flown: white characters over
 * real terrain, real sky and real haze, instead of over a flat studio
 * colour that flatters every layout equally. It is drawn behind the
 * character grid and is not interactive.
 *
 * WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not firmware data, not telemetry, not a camera
 * feed, and it never reaches the flight controller: no encoder, decoder
 * or MSP path imports this module, and osdPreviewIsolation.test.ts fails
 * the build if one ever does. Moving an element over this image changes
 * the element's CHARACTER CELL in the draft - the image contributes
 * nothing to the bytes that are written.
 *
 * WHY IT IS EMBEDDED AS A DATA URI RATHER THAN A BUNDLED FILE. The
 * project has no raster asset pipeline at all: Metro would resolve a
 * `require` of a .jpg, Vite would need an `import`, and Jest a third
 * transform - three bundler-specific paths for one picture. A data URI is
 * the one form all three already understand, so the same bytes ship to
 * the browser, to Android and into the tests with no configuration.
 *
 * The bytes below are the operator's own file, unmodified - re-encoding
 * it here (no image tooling exists in this environment) could only lose
 * quality, so it is carried verbatim.
 *
 *   source:  1080x792 baseline JPEG, 64796 bytes
 *   sha-256: 1f71096ee5c541f80b0838da1cd0627da5d4e490320648ebd948efd9eda19dbd
 */

